"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative launched in 2029 aimed at developing advanced mental health support systems using AI, including chatbots and virtual therapists, with a goal to reach 5 million users by 2035. The project has received executive budget approval of $2 million, though specific allocations have been adjusted, such as $550,000 for general project expenses and $55,000 for compliance. The team is expanding with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing. Current activities include moving from the design phase to the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, gathering R&D proposals for AI-enhanced data visualization by July 20th, and exploring partnerships with TechInnovate. Security protocols are being updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective next January."
